  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-12-25T18:18:20.231Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The way untrusted urls right now poses a security risk to users who always have it on in order to use worlds which have their own urls that also contain things like video players. A malicious user can put malicious links in a video player such as ip grabbers and have everyone connect to it.\n\nA solution to this problem would be letting world creators whitelist certain untrusted urls and not allowing any other urls to be connected to. This could be a setting for the user as well if they have a legitimate reason to use an untrusted url. Users could also be prompted before connecting to urls the same way Discord and other platforms do it with the option to whitelist. This would enhance security on the game greatly with the rise of worlds relying on untrusted urls.",
